description:
showToast and showSnackbar side effects are called directly in the render body (not inside useEffect) in two service queue components. This causes toast/snackbar notifications to fire on every re-render when the columns config is missing.
Affected Files
queue-tables-for-all-statuses.component.tsx (line 131-137) - showToast

default-queue-table.component.tsx (line 70-76) - showSnackbar

Current Behavior
When useColumns(queue, status) returns null/undefined, a toast/snackbar notification fires directly during render. This means:
It fires on EVERY re-render, not just once when the condition changes

In React Strict Mode, it fires twice

It violates React's pure render requirement (no side effects during render)

Expected Behavior
The showToast/showSnackbar calls should be wrapped in useEffect with appropriate dependencies so they fire only once when the columns config is missing, not on every re-render.
Fix
Wrap both calls in useEffect:

useEffect(() => {
  if (!columns) {
    showToast({
      title: t('invalidtableConfig', 'Invalid table configuration'),
      kind: 'warning',
      description: '...',
    });
  }
}, [columns, t]);

Problem 
In patient-admit-or-transfer-request-form.component.tsx, the finally block called wardPatientGroupDetails.mutate() without await and reset setIsSubmitting(false) before the mutation completed.
Two issues:
mutate() was not awaited — SWR cache invalidation fired and was forgotten, causing unreliable ward list re-renders and potential unhandled rejections if the component unmounted mid-mutation.

setIsSubmitting(false) ran before mutate() resolved — the submit button re-enabled while the mutation was still in-flight, allowing a user to submit again before the ward list refreshed, risking duplicate transfer requests.

The correct pattern already exists in admit-patient-button.component.tsx in the same repo:
ts
.finally(async () => { await wardPatientGroupDetails?.mutate?.(); })
This component diverged from that pattern.
Fix Changed the finally block to:
ts
.finally(async () => {
  await wardPatientGroupDetails?.mutate?.();
  setIsSubmitting(false);
});
Mutation completes fully before the button re-enables.

The dispensing app has an Active Prescriptions and All Prescriptions tab, both containing a table showing prescriptions. The table can be configured to show a location filter, allowing the user to filter prescriptions for the selection locations.
We want to be able to further configure the location behavior, by introducing a limitFilterOptionsBySessionVisitLocation config, so that:
if true, limits the location selections dropdown to only those under the ancestor visit location for the user’s session location.

limit prescriptions rows shown to locations under user session’s visit location.

For example, suppose we have 2 hospitals. Within the system, both are “Visit Locations”. If I’m logged in to a (child) location under hospital A. I only want to see prescriptions form hospital A, and that the location filter to have location options from hospital A and not hospital B.
Implementation-wise, we’d be modifying config-schema.ts :
  locationBehavior: {
    locationColumn: {
      enabled: boolean;
    };
    locationFilter: {
      enabled: boolean;
      tag: string;
      associatedPharmacyLocationAttribute: string;
    };

    limitFilterOptionsBySessionVisitLocation: boolean; // new field here
  };

Follow-up from O3-5759 (PR https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/pull/2625).
Problem
The queue wait-time column renders durations with a hardcoded "(s)" suffix instead of real pluralization:
minuteFormatted: {{minutes}} minute(s)

hourAndMinuteFormatted: {{hours}} hour(s) and {{minutes}} minute(s)

Both live in esm-service-queues-app (queue-table/components/queue-duration.component.tsx) and are the only source-code call sites of this pattern. Many generated locale catalogs also contain the "(s)" strings. Introduced in patient-management #980 (27b7ba11). The component was later moved in #1756 (53ff32c1).
Why it matters
Grammatically wrong even in English: renders 1 minute(s), 1 hour(s) and 0 minute(s).

Not localizable: languages with more than two plural forms (Polish one/few/many, Arabic, Russian, etc.) cannot be expressed with a single "(s)". These are user-facing strings that flow to Transifex.

Proposed fix
Pluralize hours and minutes independently with i18next's count option, then compose via a translatable wrapper:
const formattedMinutes = t('queueDurationMinutes', {
  count: minutes,
  defaultValue_one: '{{count}} minute',
  defaultValue_other: '{{count}} minutes',
});

const formattedDuration =
  hours > 0
    ? t('queueDurationHoursAndMinutes', '{{hours}} and {{minutes}}', {
        hours: t('queueDurationHours', {
          count: hours,
          defaultValue_one: '{{count}} hour',
          defaultValue_other: '{{count}} hours',
        }),
        minutes: formattedMinutes,
      })
    : formattedMinutes;
New key names (not the existing minuteFormatted) are deliberate: an existing unsuffixed translation shadows i18next's plural lookup until Transifex delivers the suffixed forms.
yarn extract-translations generates the expected en.json:
{
  "queueDurationHoursAndMinutes": "{{hours}} and {{minutes}}",
  "queueDurationHours_one": "{{count}} hour",
  "queueDurationHours_other": "{{count}} hours",
  "queueDurationMinutes_one": "{{count}} minute",
  "queueDurationMinutes_other": "{{count}} minutes"
}

The registration configuration allows a user to configure where to navigate after a patient is saved. The default is the patient chart. 
As we have started adding O3 apps and features to the PIH Malawi EMR, we want to have the ability to navigate to an old patient dashboard, which is a non SPA page. This is where I discovered this bug that when I try the following configuration the system resolved the URL to undefined.

"@openmrs/esm-patient-registration-app": {
  "links": {
    "submitButton": "${openmrsBase}/patientDashboard.form?patientId=${patientUuid}"
  },
  }
